Rule-development holdout (60-bug corpus). The 60-bug historical corpus was assembled by
keyword search without first inspecting any forward body; the operator catalogue was enumerated
from torch.nn.modules and torch. refs. Two leave-one-out audits are reported in the reproducibility appendix: a category-keyword LOO (no-op by design, disables orchestration modules) and
a handler-class LOO (removes the operator handlers most directly on each category’s bug path). Both
leave the aggregate RP rate at 53/60, because an independent AST-pattern verification path runs in
parallel with the operator dispatch and catches the bugs even when the per-category handlers are
disabled. Per-handler keyword attribution (load-bearing share) gives view reshape total size
and broadcasting 7 each, conv channel mismatch 6, einsum dim 5, and four further handlers
4 each; the catalogue is over-determined relative to the bug surface.
Block-corpus diversity. AST-skeleton clustering of the 488 blocks (literals→ INT , attrs→ ATTR ,
vars positionally renamed, then SHA-256 of the normalised forward body) yields Kast =406 distinct
skeletons; handler-call multiset clustering (Jaccard ≥ 0.85) yields Khandler =345. The largest cluster
has 20 members (DeepLabV3 variants); 369/406 skeletons are singletons. The 488-block corpus is
therefore not a few near-duplicates dressed in size — the effective number of distinct shape-reasoning
challenges is ≥ 345.
Importable vs. unimportable surface. On the 488-block corpus, where most blocks need a
config object, the abstention surface and the non-importable surface coincide; this is corpus-baked.
We falsify a stronger reading by building a 25-block stress set of importable, no-arg-constructor
nn.Modules selected to exercise (i) symbolic-shape refutation under a contract no concrete trace
satisfies, (ii) requires grad / detach flow, and (iii) concrete shape arithmetic recoverable only by
execution. The contingency table is Table 4: TG-only catches 20 (12 symbolic shape, 8 grad-flag);
FakeTensorMode-only catches 5 (concrete .size()-arithmetic outside the TG fragment); the two
surfaces are complementary, not coincident, on importable inputs.
