Per-feature ablation and localisation / hybrid-mode results

Real-corpus ablation . We also re-ran the five-feature ladder of Table 5 on the upstream-faithful
10-bug real corpus from Table 2. The result is a flat line at (7/10 RP@0.99, 8/10 RP@0.80 cumulative,
2/10 silent verified) for every disabled feature: none of CEGAR, device-flag, phase, grad-flow, or
low-conf gating discriminates on the real bugs. This corroborates the “stress-only” caveat already in
the caption of Table 5 with a direct empirical measurement on the real-public-repo subset.
Localisation. On a 30-item marker-only audit — repros carrying an explicit # BUG comment
as the ground-truth line, with no information shared with the AST-walk strategy — 17 of the 30
were refuted by TG with a computable distance to the marker. Of those 17, the “first unsatisfied
symbolic constraint” tracer (Section 3.3) lands within ±5 lines on 14/17 (82%) and within ±1 line
on 11/17 (65%). This is a calibration result: the tracer is accurate to the nearest few source lines
on the bugs it refutes, but the 17 computable cases are the ones TG successfully catches, so the
numerator is self-selecting. The 13 non-computable cases (no distance because TG did not refute
or returned a location.line=0 witness) are the relevant coverage gap. End-to-end fraction. The
runtime-tracer-comparable headline is therefore 14/30 = 46.7% within ±5 lines (Wilson 95% CI
[30.2%, 63.9%]), with the 14/17 = 82% figure retained as a calibration on the catches. On a per-item
analyser pass under the user-visible default configuration, all 13/13 resolve to silent-verified (no
Bug, no Abstain), and 1/13 falls in the constructor-bound integer-attribute envelope class flagged
in Section 6 (rb pf 006); the remaining 12/13 are semantically-aliased-view bugs (the upstream
and fixed view targets agree on total element count for the input shape that exercises the bug) plus
three runtime-traceback grad-flow / cross-entropy weight cases whose root cause is not in the shape
fragment. The full per-item breakdown is provided in the reproducibility appendix.
