4.4

534

We ship a Lean 4 operator-rule audit for 28 shape-transfer rules: . Each rule is defined as a total Lean
function on List Nat; all 11 previously-axiomatic soundness lemmas are now closed sorry-free by
Lean-core tactics, including the corrected in-range form permList compose inrange; the original
permList compose statement was unconditional and is false at the boundary, so we restate the
lemma in the appendix under its in-range form (the in-range restatement is sufficient for Theorem 2
because no TG forward-rule path emits a permList composition with an out-of-range index; the
out-of-range case is a Lean-internal list-default artifact, not a TG obligation; see Section I). The full
tree builds sorry-free under lake build . The audit additionally reimplements each rule as an exact
byte-mirror in Python and diffs against torch 2.9.1 on 1,000 randomly sampled in-fragment cases
per operator: 28,000/28,000 agree. The complementary boundary check samples shapes outside
each rule’s declared precondition envelope and verifies that either torch raises or the torch result
shape disagrees with the rule’s prediction; on 10 rules and ∼2,400 off-envelope samples we observe
no silent-through cases (i.e. no rule has a precondition strictly narrower than torch’s permissive
behaviour on the sampled mutators).

