For every model we record ground-truth runtime grad-flag topology (the set of
parameters with p.grad is not None after the backward pass) and compare against the
analyser’s verdict: the analyser returns R EFUTED -P ROOF on 8/8 of these scripts (its
torch.utils.checkpoint/gradient checkpointing enable detector flips them out of the
first-order grad lattice), giving a runtime false-verified rate of 0/8 = 0.0% on a trainer-realistic
harness with checkpointing enabled. This complements the 1/42 static AST-grep estimate with a
runtime measurement on the same construct family, and is a strict-zero on the harness on which an
undetected silent error would be most damaging.

