A runtime value v is a record (sh, τ, rg, ot) where sh ∈ Z∗>0 is the concrete shape tuple, τ ∈ DType,
rg ∈ B is requires grad, and ot ∈ B is is on tape. A heap σ : Var ⇀ Val maps variable names
to runtime values; σ[x 7→ v] denotes functional update. The grad context G ∈ {on, off} records
whether the cursor is inside torch.no grad(), matching the flag in Section 2.
