3. ⟨s, σ, G⟩ → ⟨E RROR, σ, G⟩, and this arises only when prec(op, v̄) fails for some operator
op in s—equivalently, when the corresponding typing-rule premise (T-M ATMUL’s k-equality,
T-V IEW (−1)’s divisibility, etc.) is not satisfied by the concrete shapes in σ.
Proof. By structural induction on the typing derivation Γ ⊢ s : τ .
Case T-R ETURN. s = return e. If e is a value, clause (a). Otherwise, locate the innermost non-value
sub-expression of e; by the grammar of FTG , it is of the form x1 .op(x̄2.. ) with all xi ∈ dom(σ). If
prec(op, σ(x̄)) holds, E-O P fires and the result propagates via E-E VAL C TX to produce a step (clause
b); if it fails, E-O P E RR fires followed by E-E VAL E RR (clause c with the named precondition failure).
Case T-A SSIGN. s = x = e ; s0 . Identical argument on e; if e is already a value, E-B IND fires
(clause b).
Case T-I F. The shape-determinism restriction ensures c is a static integer expression. Since σ |= Γ,
all shape variables in c are instantiated and c evaluates to a unique Boolean: E-I F T or E-I F F applies.
Clause (b).
Case T-F OR. The loop bound n is static in Γ and hence determined by σ; n ≥ 0 since it is a natural
number derivable from shape refinements. If n = 0, E-F OR Z applies; if n > 0, E-F OR S applies.
Clause (b).
Case T-S EQ. s = s1 ; s2 . If s1 = skip, E-S KIP applies (clause b). Otherwise the IH on s1 gives
clause (b) (a step for s1 , propagated to s1 ; s2 by the eval-context rule for sequences) or clause (c)
(an error propagated by E-E VAL E RR).
No other stuck states arise within FTG : data-dependent branches are excluded by definition; dynamic
dispatch outside Cat triggers A BSTAIN at the analysis phase and does not reach these semantics.
