D.7

Soundness Corollary

Corollary 12 (Soundness, classical form). Let s ∈ FTG with Γ ⊢ s : τ and σ |= Γ. If every operator
op reachable during reduction of ⟨s, σ, G⟩ satisfies prec(op, v̄) in σ, then no reduction sequence
raises S HAPE -M ISMATCH -E RROR.
Proof. Under the hypothesis, Theorem 11(c) never applies. Theorem 10 guarantees that each nonerror step yields a well-typed configuration (Γ′ ⊇ Γ, s′ , σ ′ ) with σ ′ |= Γ′ , so the precondition
hypothesis is maintained at every subsequent step. By induction on the length of any finite reduction
prefix, the error sink is never reached.

949

Relationship to Theorem 2. Theorem 2 (soundness of proof-grade verdicts) is the abstractinterpretation specialisation of Theorems 10 and 11 to the verdict lattice. Concretely: V ERIFIED
means Z3 has symbolically discharged prec(op, ·) for all operators under Γ, so the precondition
hypothesis of Theorem 12 holds for every σ |= Γ, yielding Theorem 2(i). R EFUTED -P ROOF witnesses
a concrete σ |= Γ in which some prec fails, so Theorem 11(c) fires at the witnessed step, giving
Theorem 2(ii). Hence Theorem 2 is exactly the pair (T heorem 10, T heorem 11) run through the
Z3 abstraction layer; the verdict lattice is the coarsened output domain.

