Assume/Guarantee proofs

959

Fresh-witness axiom for Theorem 4. The analyser emits R EFUTED -P ROOF (or C ONTRACTV IOLATION) for a module M under context Γ only if, in the current pass under Γ, it produces a
concrete input x with assume M (x) ∧ ¬guarantee M (M (x)) (i.e. cached witnesses from prior passes
do not count). Under this axiom Theorem 4 follows by case analysis on the form of refinement:
strengthening GM0 to G′M0 leaves the discharged obligation AM0 ⇒ G′M0 strictly stronger than
the prior one, so Z3 either succeeds (V ERIFIED preserved) or returns unknown/timeout (A BSTAIN);
strengthening AM0 to A′M0 shrinks the set of inputs reaching M0 and so cannot create a fresh
refutation witness. Theorem 3 follows by induction on the call-tree using S EQ, PAR, and S UB
together with Theorem 2 at each leaf.

