Shape-pattern coverage suite (catalogue-coverage check)

1030

The files are hand-distilled one-line repros of the same upstream bugs as the upstream-faithful
corpus (Table 2), reduced to a single forward(self, x): return x.view(...) call with the
divisibility-arithmetic content of the bug pre-extracted by hand. TG returns 10/10 R EFUTED -P ROOF
at confidence 0.99 on this suite. This is a catalogue-coverage sanity check — it verifies that TG’s
rule table covers each of the shape-arithmetic bug patterns once a human has already isolated them —
and is not a real-bug evaluation; the live-class result is the 7/10 + 1/10 + 2/10 triple in Table 2. We
retain the suite as a regression target for the rule catalogue (a future rule table change that silently
drops one of these patterns is detectable by re-running the suite); the headline counts in the body do
not include it.

