LW–RP gap on the 488-block corpus

Of the 78 L IBRARY-WARN verdicts on the block corpus, 66 (84.6%) are dispatch-outside-fragment
in a sense no catalogue extension would convert to R EFUTED -P ROOF: 37 classes have no forward
body in scope at all (inheritance-only stubs); 27 are subclasses of user-defined non-nn.Module
bases whose forward semantics are inherited; 2 iterate over an opaque self.<container>. The
residual 12 (15.4%) use only fragment ops in their forward bodies and are an upper bound on the
LW→RP conversions strengthening catalogue-internal reasoning could yield without enlarging the
operator-catalogue fragment. Reproducibility artefact: .

